@Valid is a standard Bean Validation annotation from Jakarta.
It simply triggers validation on an object and does not support validation groups.
It is mainly used in controllers for request bodies and DTOs.

@Validated is a Spring-specific annotation.
It supports validation groups and also enables method-level validation using AOP.
It is typically used at the service layer or class level.

👉 Key difference:
@Validated can validate method parameters, @Valid cannot.